# No codegen — user generates everything

Do **not** run, regenerate, or hand-edit **any** generated or codegen output. The user runs all generators locally.

## Never run these commands

- `build_runner` (`fvm dart run build_runner …`, `flutter pub run build_runner …`)
- `flutter gen-l10n` / intl generate / `flutter_intl` CLI
- `injectable_generator`, `freezed` codegen, `json_serializable`, or any similar generator CLI
- Do **not** run codegen to verify work, fix analyzer errors, or “finish” a task

## Never create or edit generated files

Including but not limited to:

- `*.freezed.dart`, `*.g.dart`
- `lib/di/service_locator.config.dart`
- `lib/generated/l10n.dart`, `lib/generated/intl/**`
- `GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java` / `.m` (Flutter tool output)
- Stub or partial generated files to silence analyzer errors

## What to write instead

- Source only: `@freezed` / `@injectable` / `part` directives, `.arb` keys, models, entities
- Leave missing generated parts as-is until the user runs codegen
- Wire dependencies manually (e.g. factory) if injectable output is not yet regenerated

## Expected errors until the user generates

Treat as normal — do **not** “fix” by generating or stubbing:

- Missing `part` files (`*.freezed.dart`, `*.g.dart`, `service_locator.config.dart`)
- Undefined `S.current.<newKey>` after adding `.arb` keys
- Missing GetIt registrations for newly `@injectable` types
- Analyzer errors **only** in generated files or caused solely by stale codegen

## Agent checklist

- [ ] Did not run `build_runner` or any generator CLI
- [ ] Did not edit `*.freezed.dart`, `*.g.dart`, or `service_locator.config.dart`
- [ ] Added only source files + `.arb` keys for new strings
- [ ] Mentioned once at the end (if relevant): user should run codegen when ready
